{"id":"mahabharata-3-106","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":106,"title":"षडधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 106 · Kapila burns the sons of Sagara","summary":{"en":"Insulting the meditating Kapila as the thief, the sixty thousand are burned to ashes by his glance. Sagara's grandson Amshuman humbly recovers the horse from Kapila, the sacrifice is completed, and the line passes to Dilipa.","kn":"ಧ್ಯಾನಸ್ಥ ಕಪಿಲನನ್ನು ಕಳ್ಳನೆಂದು ಅವಮಾನಿಸಿದ ಅರವತ್ತು ಸಾವಿರ ಮಂದಿ ಅವರ ದೃಷ್ಟಿಯಿಂದ ಭಸ್ಮವಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಸಗರನ ಮೊಮ್ಮಗ ಅಂಶುಮಂತನು ವಿನಯದಿಂದ ಕಪಿಲರಿಂದ ಕುದುರೆಯನ್ನು ಮರಳಿ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಯಜ್ಞ ಪೂರ್ಣವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ, ವಂಶ ದಿಲೀಪನಿಗೆ ಸಾಗುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"ध्यानमग्न कपिल को चोर कहकर अपमानित करने वाले साठ हज़ार उनकी दृष्टि से भस्म हो जाते हैं। सगर के पौत्र अंशुमान विनम्रता से कपिल से घोड़ा वापस पाते हैं, यज्ञ पूरा होता है, और वंश दिलीप तक पहुँचता है।","te":"ధ్యానంలో ఉన్న కపిలుని దొంగ అని అవమానించిన అరవై వేల మంది ఆయన చూపుకు భస్మమవుతారు. సగరుని మనవడు అంశుమంతుడు వినయంతో కపిలుని నుండి గుర్రాన్ని తిరిగి పొందుతాడు, యజ్ఞం పూర్తవుతుంది, వంశం దిలీపునికి చేరుతుంది.","ta":"தியானத்திலிருந்த கபிலரைத் திருடன் என்று இகழ்ந்த அறுபதாயிரம் பேரும் அவர் பார்வையால் சாம்பலாகிறார்கள். ஸகரனின் பேரன் அம்ஶுமான் பணிவுடன் கபிலரிடமிருந்து குதிரையை மீட்க, யாகம் நிறைவுறுகிறது; வம்சம் திலீபனுக்குச் செல்கிறது.","ml":"ധ്യാനത്തിലിരിക്കുന്ന കപിലനെ കള്ളനെന്ന് അധിക്ഷേപിച്ച അറുപതിനായിരം പേരെയും അദ്ദേഹം നോട്ടംകൊണ്ട് ചാമ്പലാക്കുന്നു. സഗരന്റെ പൗത്രനായ അംശുമാൻ വിനയത്തോടെ കപിലനിൽനിന്ന് കുതിരയെ വീണ്ടെടുക്കുന്നു, യാഗം പൂർത്തിയാകുന്നു, വംശം ദിലീപന് കൈമാറപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.106; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ते तं दृष्ट्वा हयं राजन्संप्रहृष्टतनूरुहाः ।\nअनादृत्य महात्मानं कपिलं कालचोदिताः ।\nसंक्रुद्धाः समधावन्त अश्वग्रहणकाङ्क्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the horse, king, the hair on their bodies bristled with joy; driven by fate, they scorned the great Kapila and, enraged, rushed forward wanting to seize the horse."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो महाराज कपिलो मुनिसत्तमः ।\nवासुदेवेति यं प्राहुः कपिलं मुनिसत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kapila, best of sages, whom they call Vasudeva, grew angry, great king."}},{"n":3,"text":"स चक्षुर्विवृतं कृत्वा तेजस्तेषु समुत्सृजन् ।\nददाह सुमहातेजा मन्दबुद्धीन्स सागरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Opening his eyes and sending forth his energy upon them, that sage of immense radiance burned the dull-witted Sagaras."}},{"n":4,"text":"तान्दृष्ट्वा भस्मसाद्भूतान्नारदः सुमहातपाः ।\nसगरान्तिकमागच्छत्तच्च तस्मै न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them reduced to ashes, Narada, great in austerity, came to Sagara and told him."}},{"n":5,"text":"स तच्छ्रुत्वा वचो घोरं राजा मुनिमुखोद्गतम् ।\nमुहूर्तं विमना भूत्वा स्थाणोर्वाक्यमचिन्तयत् ।\nआत्मानमात्मनाश्वास्य हयमेवान्वचिन्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that dreadful news from the sage's mouth, the king was for a moment dejected and thought of Sthanu's words; consoling himself, he turned his thoughts to the horse."}},{"n":6,"text":"अंशुमन्तं समाहूय असमञ्जःसुतं तदा ।\nपौत्रं भरतशार्दूल इदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, tiger of the Bharatas, he summoned his grandson Amshuman, son of Asamanja, and said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"षष्टिस्तानि सहस्राणि पुत्राणाममितौजसाम् ।\nकापिलं तेज आसाद्य मत्कृते निधनं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sixty thousand sons of boundless might have met their deaths on my account, meeting Kapila's fire."}},{"n":8,"text":"तव चापि पिता तात परित्यक्तो मयानघ ।\nधर्मं संरक्षमाणेन पौराणां हितमिच्छता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And your father too, dear boy, was cast out by me, blameless one, as I kept to dharma and wished for the welfare of the townspeople.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"किमर्थं राजशार्दूलः सगरः पुत्रमात्मजम् ।\nत्यक्तवान्दुस्त्यजं वीरं तन्मे ब्रूहि तपोधन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ascetic, tell me why the tiger among kings, Sagara, abandoned his own son, a hero hard to abandon."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"असमञ्जा इति ख्यातः सगरस्य सुतो ह्यभूत् ।\nयं शैब्या जनयामास पौराणां स हि दारकान् ।\nखुरेषु क्रोशतो गृह्य नद्यां चिक्षेप दुर्बलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sagara's son, born of Shaibya, was known as Asamanja. He used to seize the children of the townspeople as they screamed, and throw the weak ones into the river."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततः पौराः समाजग्मुर्भयशोकपरिप्लुताः ।\nसगरं चाभ्ययाचन्त सर्वे प्राञ्जलयः स्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the townspeople came together, swamped by fear and grief, and all stood with joined hands and begged Sagara."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्वं नस्त्राता महाराज परचक्रादिभिर्भयैः ।\nअसमञ्जोभयाद्घोरात्ततो नस्त्रातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Great king, you are our saviour from enemy armies and other fears; so save us from the dreadful fear of Asamanja.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"पौराणां वचनं श्रुत्वा घोरं नृपतिसत्तमः ।\nमुहूर्तं विमना भूत्वा सचिवानिदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the townspeople's terrible plea, the best of kings was for a moment dejected and said to his ministers,"}},{"n":14,"text":"असमञ्जाः पुरादद्य सुतो मे विप्रवास्यताम् ।\nयदि वो मत्प्रियं कार्यमेतच्छीघ्रं विधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let my son Asamanja be banished from the city today. If you wish to please me, do this at once.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"एवमुक्ता नरेन्द्रेण सचिवास्ते नराधिप ।\nयथोक्तं त्वरिताश्चक्रुर्यथाज्ञापितवान्नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told so by the king, the ministers quickly did it as the king had commanded."}},{"n":16,"text":"एतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं यथा पुत्रो महात्मना ।\nपौराणां हितकामेन सगरेण विवासितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this I have told you, how Sagara, wishing his people well, banished his son."}},{"n":17,"text":"अंशुमांस्तु महेष्वासो यदुक्तः सगरेण ह ।\nतत्ते सर्वं प्रवक्ष्यामि कीर्त्यमानं निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now I will tell you all that Sagara said to the great archer Amshuman; listen as I recount it."}},{"text":"सगर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sagara said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"पितुश्च तेऽहं त्यागेन पुत्राणां निधनेन च ।\nअलाभेन तथाश्वस्य परितप्यामि पुत्रक ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear boy, I am tormented by your father's banishment, by my sons' deaths, and by not recovering the horse."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्माद्दुःखाभिसंतप्तं यज्ञविघ्नाच्च मोहितम् ।\nहयस्यानयनात्पौत्र नरकान्मां समुद्धर ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, grandson, rescue me from hell, tormented by grief and bewildered by this obstacle to my sacrifice, by bringing back the horse."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"अंशुमानेवमुक्तस्तु सगरेण महात्मना ।\nजगाम दुःखात्तं देशं यत्र वै दारिता मही ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this by the great Sagara, Amshuman went in sorrow to the place where the earth was split."}},{"n":21,"text":"स तु तेनैव मार्गेण समुद्रं प्रविवेश ह ।\nअपश्यच्च महात्मानं कपिलं तुरगं च तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that same path he entered the sea, and saw the great Kapila and that horse."}},{"n":22,"text":"स दृष्ट्वा तेजसो राशिं पुराणमृषिसत्तमम् ।\nप्रणम्य शिरसा भूमौ कार्यमस्मै न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that mass of radiance, the ancient best of sages, he bowed his head to the ground and told him his purpose."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः प्रीतो महातेजाः कलिपोंऽशुमतोऽभवत् ।\nउवाच चैनं धर्मात्मा वरदोऽस्मीति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty Kapila was pleased with Amshuman, and that righteous one said to him, \"I will grant a boon,\" Bharata."}},{"n":24,"text":"स वव्रे तुरगं तत्र प्रथमं यज्ञकारणात् ।\nद्वितीयमुदकं वव्रे पितॄणां पावनेप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Amshuman first chose the horse, for the sake of the sacrifice, and second he chose water for the ancestors, wishing to purify them."}},{"n":25,"text":"तमुवाच महातेजाः कपिलो मुनिपुंगवः ।\nददानि तव भद्रं ते यद्यत्प्रार्थयसेऽनघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great Kapila, best of sages, said to him: \"Blameless one, I will give you whatever you ask. May you prosper."}},{"n":26,"text":"त्वयि क्षमा च धर्मश्च सत्यं चापि प्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nत्वया कृतार्थः सगरः पुत्रवांश्च त्वया पिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In you forbearance, dharma and truth are established. Through you Sagara has achieved his aim, and through you your father has a son."}},{"n":27,"text":"तव चैव प्रभावेन स्वर्गं यास्यन्ति सागराः ।\nपौत्रश्च ते त्रिपथगां त्रिदिवादानयिष्यति ।\nपावनार्थं सागराणां तोषयित्वा महेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By your power the Sagaras will go to heaven, and your grandson will bring down the three-pathed Ganga from heaven to purify the Sagaras, after pleasing Maheshvara."}},{"n":28,"text":"हयं नयस्व भद्रं ते यज्ञियं नरपुंगव ।\nयज्ञः समाप्यतां तात सगरस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Take the horse, good fortune to you, the sacrificial animal, best of men. Let the sacrifice of the great Sagara be completed.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"अंशुमानेवमुक्तस्तु कपिलेन महात्मना ।\nआजगाम हयं गृह्य यज्ञवाटं महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the great Kapila, Amshuman took the horse and came to the great king's sacrificial ground."}},{"n":30,"text":"सोऽभिवाद्य ततः पादौ सगरस्य महात्मनः ।\nमूर्ध्नि तेनाप्युपाघ्रातस्तस्मै सर्वं न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saluted the great Sagara's feet, and kissed on the head by him, told him everything,"}},{"n":31,"text":"यथा दृष्टं श्रुतं चापि सागराणां क्षयं तथा ।\nतं चास्मै हयमाचष्ट यज्ञवाटमुपागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"what he had seen and heard, and the destruction of the Sagaras, and showed him the horse that had come to the sacrifice."}},{"n":32,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा सगरो राजा पुत्रजं दुःखमत्यजत् ।\nअंशुमन्तं च संपूज्य समापयत तं क्रतुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that, King Sagara put away his grief for his sons, honoured Amshuman, and completed the sacrifice."}},{"n":33,"text":"समाप्तयज्ञः सगरो देवैः सर्वैः सभाजितः ।\nपुत्रत्वे कल्पयामास समुद्रं वरुणालयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sacrifice done, Sagara was honoured by all the gods, and he made the sea, Varuna's abode, his son."}},{"n":34,"text":"प्रशास्य सुचिरं कालं राज्यं राजीवलोचनः ।\nपौत्रे भारं समावेश्य जगाम त्रिदिवं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lotus-eyed king ruled for a very long time, then placed the burden on his grandson and went to heaven."}},{"n":35,"text":"अंशुमानपि धर्मात्मा महीं सागरमेखलाम् ।\nप्रशशास महाराज यथैवास्य पितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The righteous Amshuman too ruled the earth, girdled by the sea, just as his grandfather had, great king."}},{"n":36,"text":"तस्य पुत्रः समभवद्दिलीपो नाम धर्मवित् ।\nतस्मै राज्यं समाधाय अंशुमानपि संस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His son was named Dilipa, a knower of dharma, and after entrusting the kingdom to him Amshuman also died."}},{"n":37,"text":"दिलीपस्तु ततः श्रुत्वा पितॄणां निधनं महत् ।\nपर्यतप्यत दुःखेन तेषां गतिमचिन्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dilipa, hearing of the great destruction of his forefathers, was tormented by grief and thought of their fate."}},{"n":38,"text":"गङ्गावतरणे यत्नं सुमहच्चाकरोन्नृपः ।\nन चावतारयामास चेष्टमानो यथाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king made great efforts to bring the Ganga down, but though he tried with all his strength he could not bring her down."}},{"n":39,"text":"तस्य पुत्रः समभवच्छ्रीमान्धर्मपरायणः ।\nभगीरथ इति ख्यातः सत्यवागनसूयकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had a glorious son devoted to dharma, named Bhagiratha, truthful in speech and free of envy."}},{"n":40,"text":"अभिषिच्य तु तं राज्ये दिलीपो वनमाश्रितः ।\nतपःसिद्धिसमायोगात्स राजा भरतर्षभ ।\nवनाज्जगाम त्रिदिवं कालयोगेन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dilipa consecrated him as king and went to the forest, and through the accomplishment of austerity that king, best of Bharatas, went from the forest to heaven in due time."}}]}]}